BIT-14: Write the report and copy the output file in blocks; format numbers without printf

MSXsaveoutfile() copied the output file one byte at a time; the report
read every value back from the output file with its own seek and 4-byte
read; report lines were built with strcat; and every value went through
sprintf. Copy and read in blocks, append to the line directly, and format
concentrations with a formatter of its own that gives the same text,
calling sprintf for the rare values that sit exactly on a rounding tie.

Requires: none
Results: identical (every concentration, the output file and the report are unchanged)

Apply from the root of an EPANET-MSX checkout at 85a303d, after FIX-01, FIX-02 and BIT-01 to BIT-13:
    git apply --whitespace=nowarn BIT-14.patch
or use tools/build-msx.sh, which applies the series in order.

